```

Each model independently calls the same production repository tools against a frozen evidence set. The result is rendered as a grid of `<article>` cards:

```tsx
// frontend/src/components/AskWorkspace.tsx  lines 438–478
{comparison.runs.map((run) => (
  <article key={`${run.provider}:${run.model}`}>
    <strong>{run.provider}:{run.model}</strong>
    <small>{run.repository_tool_calls} tools · {run.total_model_rounds} rounds · …s</small>
    <dl>
      <div><dt>Hit@5</dt><dd>{(run.candidate_retrieval.hit_at_5 * 100).toFixed(0)}%</dd></div>
      <div><dt>MRR</dt><dd>{run.candidate_retrieval.mrr.toFixed(3)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>nDCG@10</dt><dd>{run.candidate_retrieval.ndcg_at_10.toFixed(3)}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Tokens</dt><dd>{run.total_tokens ?? "n/a"}</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <ol>
      {run.candidate_retrieval.ranked_paths.slice(0, 10).map((path) => (
        <li key={path}>{path}</li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </article>
))}
```

Metrics shown per model: Hit@5, MRR, nDCG@10, token count, tool calls, rounds, and the top-10 ranked candidate paths. If expected paths were supplied in the optional input field, the scores are objective; otherwise the panel notes "Trajectory-only."

